This is an optional regression module, excluded from normal firmware/package builds.
It calls the real OSAL and Linux kernel APIs; it does not emulate their implementation.

Build against the exact prepared kernel and OSAL source used by the target:

  make -C "$KDIR" ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-openwrt-linux-musl- \
    M="$PWD/package/mtk/drivers/mt_wifi_osal/tests" OSAL_SRC="$OSAL_SRC" \
    KBUILD_EXTRA_SYMBOLS="$OSAL_SRC/Module.symvers" modules

On an isolated test board, unload other OSAL consumers first and load the matching
mt_wifi_osal.ko, then mt_wifi_osal_regression.ko. The tests temporarily own OSAL
device slot 1. They run at module insertion and report each result to the kernel
log; an error causes insertion to fail. Unload the regression module afterwards.

Cases cover RX checksum equivalence with skb_pull_rcsum, VLAN wire order, calendar
and boottime units, nonzero kthread exit, delayed-work cancellation/requeue,
running-timer synchronization (SMP), and completion of queued RCU callbacks.

Compilation does not execute these checks. This module does not validate WiFi RF,
throughput, NETDEV unregister under cfg80211, or FIPS daemon protocol behavior.
